---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import ProductCallout from '../components/ProductCallout.astro';
import EmailOptin from '../components/EmailOptin.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Buzzyfly — Built by someone who actually runs it"
	description="Why Buzzyfly exists, who built it, and why the Digital System is worth $49."
	pubDate={new Date('August 15 2026')}
	heroImage="/buzzyfly-brand-about.jpg"
>
	<p>
		Buzzyfly started from a familiar problem: too many tools, and nothing holding them
		together. I'd spend a slow morning setting up a clean process, feel good about it for
		about a week, and then watch it quietly fall apart the moment things got busy — a new
		client, a launch, a rough week. The tools were never really the problem. The lack of one
		place tying them together was.
	</p>

	<h2>Who's behind it</h2>
	<p>
		I'm the person who got tired of rebuilding onboarding from memory every time a client
		showed up. Tired of follow-ups dying in the inbox. Tired of the weekly reset that
		collapsed by Thursday. So I built the system I actually use to run my own shop — then
		packaged it so you don't have to start from zero.
	</p>
	<p>
		I run Buzzyfly the way I'd want a tool I paid for to be run: I use what I sell, I fix
		what breaks, and if part of the system doesn't hold up under real use, it gets rebuilt
		instead of just re-explained in nicer language.
	</p>

	<h2>What you actually get</h2>
	<p>
		The Buzzyfly Digital System is a small, opinionated set of workflows for the parts of
		running a business that eat the most time and get the least credit — onboarding, weekly
		planning, and following up — built so they still hold up on the days you don't feel like
		running them. Checklists and templates you open, tick, and close. Not a 200-tab
		spreadsheet you'll never touch again.
	</p>

	<h2>Why people buy it</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Onboarding that doesn't live in your head anymore</li>
		<li>Follow-ups that actually get sent instead of rotting</li>
		<li>A weekly reset that survives a slammed Thursday</li>
		<li>Scope-creep scripts so you stop giving work away for free</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>The guarantee</h2>
	<p>
		7-day email refund if the files aren't what the store lists. No hoops, no guilt trip.
		If it doesn't fit how you work, you get your money back.
	</p>

	<ProductCallout />

	<EmailOptin
		title="Want the free weekly reset checklist first?"
		description="Send me the 20-minute version. No spam. Just the checklist, plus one email a week with the next piece of the system."
		buttonLabel="Send me the checklist"
	/>

	<p>
		Questions, feedback, or something broken? Reach out — this is a small operation and
		real notes from real users are how it gets better.
	</p>
</Layout>
